implementationPlan.description:
Adversarial self-review: load the adversarial-self-review skill.

Mutation sweep:
- Work only on scratch full-tree archive copies, never the shared tree. Use one mutant per copy.
- Run each with `timeout 120` and --test-name-pattern='^(AE[12]|LA[1-6]|SH[1-9]|TY[1-3]) ', and score by exit code.
- Put a per-run env marker in the node env, so you kill only your own leftover python processes. Never `pgrep -af guest-supervisor`: agent prompts contain that string (mem gotcha-local-runner-supervisor-tests).
- An AE row must kill each of these:
  (a) guest-supervisor.py LAUNCH codex config without its env_vars line;
  (b) LAUNCH claude tail plus '--continue';
  (c) LAUNCH claude config with a second mcpServers entry;
  (d) SHIM naming another path;
  (e) start_job spawning with cwd = home instead of workspace;
  (f) guest-mcp-shim.py main() serving the worker table whatever MOE_ROLE says;
  (g) the shim's tool-allowlist check removed: the call then reaches the host, comes back as REFUSED BRIDGE_TOOL_DENIED instead of TOOL_DENIED, and AE1 kills it;
  (h) the shim's argument-key check removed: AE1 gets BRIDGE_IDENTITY_MISMATCH instead of ARGUMENT_DENIED;
  (i) install_agents without its sha256 comparison (AE2);
  (j) JOBS['codex'] moved to /opt/moe/bin/codex (AE2 layout, and AE1 codex).
- Record each kill and the counts in the step note. For any survivor, prove it is equivalent or add an assertion.

Then confirm, and record each in the note:
- this task changed only scripts/tests/local-runner-bridge.test.mjs;
- every pre-existing row is byte-identical (the diff is additions only);
- 300 changed lines or fewer;
- ASCII only (grep -cP '[^\x00-\x7f]');
- no __pycache__ under scripts/local-runner;
- no leftover processes from your runs;
- nothing makes executionReady true or claims verified-local or isolation.

If the review changed any byte, re-run the step-3 command fresh and submit that output instead.

